{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.partialSum_not_monotone_of_term_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.partialSum_not_monotone_of_term_neg","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationSignObstruction.lean#L74-L79","doc":"The extensivity conclusion itself needs every term non-negative; one\nnegative term breaks monotonicity of the partial sums at that order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.not_forall_aD_nonneg_of_term_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.not_forall_aD_nonneg_of_term_neg","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationSignObstruction.lean#L66-L72","doc":"**The hypothesis is not merely unverified but false, given one negative\nterm.** Stated in the `_of_` conditional style: IF some body-order term is\nnegative and `w` is structurally non-negative, THEN `∀ n, 0 ≤ aD n` fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.aD_neg_of_term_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.aD_neg_of_term_neg","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationSignObstruction.lean#L57-L64","doc":"**A negative body-order term forces a negative `a_D`.** Since `w n ≥ 0` is\nstructural, an alternation observed in the product is carried by `a_D` alone:\nthe jet-filtration hypothesis fails in its `a_D` half, never its `w` half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.term","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.term","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationSignObstruction.lean#L54-L55","doc":"The body-order term. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.wOf_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.wOf_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationSignObstruction.lean#L48-L52","doc":"**`w` is non-negative structurally**, from the non-negativity of a count and\nof a volume. This is the half of the hypothesis that cannot fail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.wOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.JetFiltrationSignObstruction.wOf","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/JetFiltrationSignObstruction.lean#L45-L46","doc":"`w n = M n * Vol n`: a coordination multiplicity times a hyperbolic volume. ","signatureChunk":0}]}